Fluid (R3) SoundFont
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files:      device/samples/gm/*/*.flac
Author:     Frank Wen, with the contributors named in its README
Copyright:  Copyright (c) 2000-2002, 2008 Frank Wen
License:    MIT
Source:     FluidR3_GM.sf2, as packaged in Debian and Ubuntu (fluid-soundfont-gm 3.1),
            first published at http://www.musescore.org/download/fluid-soundfont.tar.gz
Changes:    15 voices (one for each General MIDI family apart from the piano) and the
            drum kit, played note by note through FluidSynth with no reverb or chorus,
            every fourth semitone, cut to a few seconds, made mono, leveled per
            voice and stored as 16 bit FLAC at 48 kHz. Used as the other voices and
            the drums of the Armonico Pi device.
Details:    device/samples/gm/SOURCE.md

